# Folder structure

Physical layout is part of the architecture contract. Agents and humans must know **where new code goes** before they invent a parallel tree. Logical layers ([`architecture`](./architecture.mdc) · [`clean-ddd-hexagonal`](../skills/clean-ddd-hexagonal/SKILL.md)) and role suffixes ([`custom-validators`](./custom-validators.mdc)) sit on top of this map — they do not replace it.

Deep template + section checklist → [`../references/engineering/folder-structure.md`](../references/engineering/folder-structure.md).

**Split of concerns:** [`clean-ddd-hexagonal`](../skills/clean-ddd-hexagonal/SKILL.md) decides layer / port / aggregate placement; **this rule** decides path, naming, and blueprint enforcement. Layer-shaped trees are one principle below — use them when the backend earns Clean/Hex/DDD; still document the real disk map here.

## When to consult / refresh the map

| Situation | Action |
| --------- | ------ |
| First session in an unfamiliar repo | Detect shape → read or draft the durable layout doc |
| New package / app / bounded context | Extend the map; do not invent a second convention |
| New feature / component / service | Follow placement + naming from the map (or templates in it) |
| Structural refactor | Update the map in the same change set as the move |
| Review of new paths | Diff against the map + role-suffix allow-list |

## Detect shape (before assuming layout)

Scan markers — do not guess from one file:

| Signal | Look for |
| ------ | -------- |
| **Language / runtime** | Manifests (`package.json`, `pyproject.toml`, `*.csproj`, `pom.xml`, `go.mod`, `Cargo.toml`, …) |
| **Monorepo** | Workspaces (`pnpm-workspace`, npm/bun workspaces), Turbo/Nx/Lerna, multiple apps under `apps/` / `packages/` |
| **Frontend** | `public/` / `static/`, UI framework configs, `components` / `pages` / `app` trees |
| **Multi-service** | Repeated service roots, per-service Dockerfiles, gateway / broker config |
| **Generated / vendor** | `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `build/`, `.next/`, `bin/`, `obj/` — exclude from the human map unless the team opts in |

Record detected shape in the durable doc (or repo-root `AGENTS.md` **Repo map**). Prefer facts over aspirational trees.

## Organizational principles (pick and stick)

Document which principle organizes **most** of the tree — mixed trees need an explicit seam:

| Principle | Folders group by… | Typical when |
| --------- | ----------------- | ------------ |
| **Layer** | `domain/` · `application/` · `infrastructure/` · `presentation/` | Hex / clean backends — pair with [`clean-ddd-hexagonal`](../skills/clean-ddd-hexagonal/SKILL.md) · [`architecture`](./architecture.mdc) · [`layers`](../references/engineering/layers.md) |
| **Feature / vertical** | Feature name owns UI + API + tests nearby | Product UIs, modular monoliths |
| **Domain / bounded context** | Context root, then layers inside | Multi-context monorepos — [`ddd-strategic`](../references/engineering/ddd-strategic.md) + clean-ddd layers per context |
| **Type** | `components/`, `hooks/`, `utils/` | Small apps only — does not scale; avoid for new large surfaces |

Repeated subtrees (every package same inner layout) are a feature — name the pattern once.

## Durable blueprint (required for non-trivial repos)

Keep one living doc the team actually updates (example paths: `docs/engineering/folder-structure.md`, `docs/design-monorepo.md`, or a section of root `AGENTS.md` **Repo map**). Minimum contents:

1. **Overview** — principles, monorepo/service relationships
2. **Visualization** — ASCII tree, nested list, or path table (depth enough to show seams; skip generated dirs by default)
3. **Key directories** — purpose + content types + conventions per significant path
4. **File placement** — where configs, models/DTOs, business logic, ports, tests, docs land
5. **Naming** — file/folder case, role suffixes, module/namespace ↔ path mapping
6. **Workflow** — entrypoints; where to add a feature / test / config change
7. **Extension templates** (optional) — skeleton folders for new feature / component / service / test tree
8. **Enforcement** — which validators or CI structure gates exist ([`ci-taxonomy`](./ci-taxonomy.mdc) Structure)

Stamp **last updated** when the tree changes.

## Placement & naming (agent defaults)

When the durable doc is missing or silent:

- Prefer **existing sibling paths** over new top-level folders
- One architectural role per file when the repo uses dotted suffixes ([`custom-validators`](./custom-validators.mdc))
- Cross-package imports only through published `public-api` (or equivalent) — [`architecture`](./architecture.mdc)
- Co-locate tests with the convention already in use (colocate `*.test` vs `tests/` mirror) — do not mix styles in one package
- Config / policy values: externalize per [`lint-strategy`](./lint-strategy.mdc); do not scatter env reads into deep packages

## Enforcement

| Layer | Mechanism |
| ----- | --------- |
| Docs | Durable blueprint + ADRs for intentional layout changes |
| Diff review | New paths must match map or get an explicit map update |
| Automated | Structure / naming / import-boundary validators ([`custom-validators`](./custom-validators.mdc)); registry checks in monorepos |
| Agents | Treat layout drift like contract drift — fix path or amend the map; ⊥ silent second tree |

No structure gate in CI yet? Review still owns new paths ([`ci-taxonomy`](./ci-taxonomy.mdc) § Adapt when missing).

